  "title": "recent: Remove some old transitional backwards compatibility code",
  "description": "When the \"recent_common\" (GUI settings common to all profiles) file was\nsplit off from \"recent\" and some settings moved to the new file, there\nwas some code added to attempt to read the moved settings from the original\nrecent file if the new recent_common file didn't exist. This proved to\nbe confusing to other people reading the code, as the comment above shows.\nIt also confuses Clang static analysis, because the fopen isn't checked for\nfailure, since it just succeeded in opening the same file at the outer\nloop (though for transient reasons it could always fail the second time,\nI reckon.)\n\nThat was 17 years ago, so it's unlikely that there are users who lack a\nrecent common file and still have a 17 year old recent file with the moved\nsettings.\n\nSee d123a61162eb935eec397d809d1002011d25d145\nand d182dfab2192f50f32b855e5d618815305989931\nand 633a53619aefa45aac40275b862dab0a9b87a518",
